//! An HTTP client, in the browser: requests go through `fetch` once the
//! policy allows `Net(host:port)`. Unlike other builds, a response from
//! another site is readable only if the site allows it (CORS), with only the
//! headers it exposes; the browser sets some request headers itself (`host`,
//! `cookie`, `user-agent`, ...) and sends no cookies; redirects fail with
//! kind `"http"`, as the browser hides where they lead; host names are
//! checked as written, not their addresses; there is no `upload` or
//! server; and every body is read whole, also for `open`, so one larger
//! than `max_http_body` fails with kind `"limit"`.

import io
import json
